// StoreServiceServer is the server API for StoreService service.
// All implementations must embed UnimplementedStoreServiceServer
// for forward compatibility.
//
// Protocol contract for plugin authors (any language).
//
// Transactions
//
//	BeginTx returns a tx_id; Commit or Rollback ends it. Send the tx_id on
//	every call that belongs to the transaction. A BeginTx with parent_tx_id
//	opens a nested transaction (a savepoint): rolling it back undoes only the
//	inner work. A transaction tree is a stack: a transaction has at most one
//	open nested transaction, and only the innermost one accepts calls and
//	Commit. Rolling back an ancestor rolls back the chain below it first.
//	Misuse is reported in the response's `error` as KIND_UNSPECIFIED with a
//	message: an unknown or already finished tx_id ("unknown or finished
//	transaction"), and a call or Commit on a transaction that has an open
//	nested one ("has an open nested transaction"). Each tree has one 60
//	second idle timer, restarted by any call in the tree; when it fires the
//	root and everything nested in it are rolled back. A plugin that exits
//	abandons its open transactions; its database rolls them back when the
//	connection drops. The host never retries across the boundary.
//
// Units
//
//	Every int64 that holds a lifetime, timeout or leeway counts SECONDS
//	(session_lifetime, token_lifetime, leeway, ...). The one exception is
//	RefreshTokensRotateRequest.leeway and ProtectionLimit intervals use
//	google.protobuf.Duration. Instants
//	are google.protobuf.Timestamp with nanosecond precision.
//
// JSON fields
//
//	custom_text_json is a JSON object: prompt -> language -> screen -> key ->
//	text, every level an object and every leaf a string. user_metadata_json
//	and app_metadata_json are each any JSON object (nested objects, arrays, strings, numbers, booleans,
//	null); numbers are read back as double-precision floats. An absent
//	optional field means "nil", which is distinct from an empty object.
//
// Absent fields (plugins older than the consent fields)
//
//	Client.is_first_party absent = true; Client.skip_non_verifiable_callback_
//	uri_confirmation_prompt absent = nil (inherit the tenant);
//	ResourceServer.skip_consent_for_verifiable_first_party_clients absent =
//	true; ClientGrant.subject_type empty = "client". A host sends
//	ClientGrantsFindRequest.subject_type; a plugin that ignores it may return
//	a grant of the other type, which the host treats as not found.
//
// Evolution
//
//	Within v1, fields are only added, never renumbered or reused. A plugin
//	that predates a field drops it silently. New RPCs may be added; a plugin
//	that lacks one answers with gRPC status Unimplemented, which the host
//	reports as an error.
//
// StoreService mirrors zeroauthy's store.Store. Every request carries tx_id:
// empty means "no transaction"; otherwise the call runs inside the
// transaction BeginTx returned. Domain errors are reported in the response's
// `error` field; gRPC status codes mean transport or plugin failure.
